# Swift Reconfiguration has flash and enchants any creature, Bot2's included. Bot2 attacks with Sundial, Dawn Tyrant (a 3/3
# Legendary Artifact Creature - Construct); Bot1 flashes the Aura onto it. It becomes an artifact Vehicle and no longer a
# creature, so it is removed from combat (CR 506.4, the ruling) and Bot1 takes no damage. The new subtype Vehicle replaces
# Construct, an artifact it keeps and the legendary supertype stays (CR 205.1a, 613.1d).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Swift Reconfiguration
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Sundial, Dawn Tyrant
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sundial, Dawn Tyrant.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Sundial, Dawn Tyrant > Bot1)
Bot1.Hand.Swift Reconfiguration.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sundial, Dawn Tyrant)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Sundial, Dawn Tyrant.Types = Artifact
